<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2885" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Antĭphătes</span></b> ,
		ae, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀντιφάτης</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A king of the Lœstrygones</i>, <i>who sunk the fleet of the Greeks returning from Troy
				with Ulysses</i>, <i>and devoured one of his
				companions</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 14, 234 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 14,
			20</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sil. 8, 531</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A son of Sarpedon</i>, <i>slain by
				Turnus</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 9, 696</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
